/-!
# Factor rigidity in the binary-block branch of 1.3.8

The global He bridge proves that Z(X) is a two-group, that X/Z(X) has
trivial center, and that the actual factor WZ(X) has odd trace P ∩ K.
It also discharges the O₂,₃ fitting-group condition of C.1.9. The exact
finite-family A.1.15 parameter is applied to a multiplication isomorphism
and its quotient factors are pulled back to the ambient subgroups.

The concrete factor-pair theorem assembles commutation of the actual conjugate
blocks and direct indecomposability of both quotient factors. It constructs
t ∈ N_T(P) outside N_T(K), identifies W = O²(X ∩ K), and proves that each
element of N_G(X) fixes or swaps WZ(X) and WᵗZ(X), with P ∩ WZ(X) = P ∩ K.
A.1.15 and C.1.9 remain explicit universally quantified source parameters;
all their local premises are discharged from the configuration and He bridge.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, proof of
1.3.8, printed p.514; A.1.15, p.23; C.1.9, p.123.
-/
